help: the trait `stack_encrypt::scalar::sealed::OneValue` is not implemented for `Profile`
  --> tests/ui/opaque_blob_requires_the_wrapper.rs:10:1
   |
10 | struct Profile {
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: to be encrypted into one `Ciphertext`, a type must meet three conditions.
   = note: first, its value must be one scalar, such as a `String`, a `bool`, a float, a `Vec<u8>`, or a fixed-width integer other than `u8`. A newtype that derives `Encrypt` over a scalar is a scalar too.
   = note: second, the value must be owned. A borrow, such as a `&str`, is not owned.
   = note: third, the type must implement `Zeroize`, so that the value can be wiped after it is encrypted.
   = note: a value that is not one scalar needs another call. `EncryptInto` encrypts each element of a `Vec` into its own `Ciphertext`. `keyset.encrypt_tree` encrypts an `Option` or a struct into a tree of ciphertexts. `OpaqueBlob` encrypts a whole `Serialize` value into one `Ciphertext`.
